ormed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3728312390","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114771#issuecomment-3728312390","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114771","id":3728312390,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eOYhG","user":{"login":"mythridium","id":132613374,"node_id":"U_kgDOB-eE_g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132613374?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mythridium","html_url":"https://github.com/mythridium","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mythridium/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mythridium/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mythridium/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mythridium/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mythridium/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mythridium/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mythridium/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mythridium/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mythridium/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T10:27:05Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T10:27:05Z","body":"This is where I got confused with that part of the documentation, because `\"[url=res://application/application.gd:10]test[/url]\"` does work with `print_rich`, it outputs with the different title and it is clickable taking me to file in the text editor, it's just when it goes into the file log that it's not stripping the url portion to leave only the title. That hint to me didn't really refer to file logging, so I was confused what it was actually referring to, as clicking the link in the output works perfectly with alternate titles.\n\nCorrect, the PR I linked has nothing to do with stripping the log output, this PR added the functionality to be able to click the url links in the output log. I guess I was merely pointing out that urls in `print_rich` is a supported thing, but perhaps the file logging portion was overlooked in either that PR or perhaps the original implementation of `print_rich` rendering url bbcodes.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3728312390/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3770609171","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114771#issuecomment-3770609171","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114771","id":3770609171,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gvu4T","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T01:12:29Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T01:34:33Z","body":"Currently, BBCode tags that are unknown to `print_rich()` are not stripped by that function. This should probably be implemented, so that file logging and custom loggers receive readable output. File logging and custom loggers strip ANSI escape codes, but they don't touch BBCode tags.\n\nIn the named `url` case, this can be implemented as well (so that the tag can be stripped with the current implementation). Terminal support for it isn't as widespread as features like truecolor, but it's improved a lot since `print_rich()` was first implemented in 2022.\n\nThe `print_rich()` implementation is here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/dc57cd698d29915cd020b1c229735e4a7ec18b7d/core/string/print_string.cpp#L100-L299","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3770609171/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]